WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:02.580
This is fast!

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:03.620
Might this be the

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:06.300
next revolution in urban travel?

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.260
Welcome to Capital Bikeshare.

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.660
Even better than the excellent bike-sharing programs

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:14.300
that cities allowed recently?

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.460
These bike share bikes are great, but

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.900
you’ve got to pick them up in the dock here

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.380
and return them to the dock,

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.300
and just putting these docks in

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:25.740
costs hundreds of thousands of dollars.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.979
As so often happens, entrepreneurs invented something

00:00:28.979 --> 00:00:31.700
even better than bikes that must be locked

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.329
into a dock.

00:00:33.329 --> 00:00:35.469
Dockless bicycles!

00:00:35.469 --> 00:00:36.773
Check out the bike,

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:38.280
take it anywhere,

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.660
and just

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:41.900
leave the thing.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:47.120
But just as I got used to dockless bicycles,

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:49.400
companies like Bird and Lime invented

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.040
still another option:

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.520
electric scooters that people can share.

00:00:54.539 --> 00:00:57.640
They’ve scooted onto streets across the country.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.880
It’s like a watered-down version of a motorcycle.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.340
A new two-wheeled battery powered way to get around.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:08.280
Yeah, that’s what I'm talking about.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:09.600
To unlock a scooter,

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.380
you just use an app on your phone.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.100
For 2 bucks I can jump on one of these things,

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.520
go where I need to go,

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:19.400
and then just

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:20.220
leave it

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:21.720
anywhere!

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.440
It stays here until someone else rents it.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:25.920
Won’t it be stolen?

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.720
No, because if someone tries to steal,

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.240
the brakes lock up,

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.620
and this happens.

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.977
"Please unlock me to ride me

00:01:34.977 --> 00:01:36.760
or I’ll call the police."

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.520
If the thief took one anyway,

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:45.360
a GPS device inside the scooter would lead police

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:46.580
right to the thief.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:49.640
The leave-the-scooter-anywhere system works.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.332
It's a new twist on old technology,

00:01:51.332 --> 00:01:53.543
that entrepreneurs found to give us something

00:01:53.543 --> 00:01:54.780
that works even better

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.060
to solve needs in dense urban areas.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.789
That’s a wonderful thing…

00:01:58.789 --> 00:02:00.340
if they don’t stop it!

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.600
By “they”, I mean, politicians.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.880
Many cities banned the scooters.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.200
A Bay Area city at war.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.740
San Francisco said:

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:10.840
"they endanger public health and safety”.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.400
Broken bones, bruises,

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:13.959
and near misses by these scooters.

00:02:13.959 --> 00:02:16.560
At 17 miles an hour – it hurts!

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.709
Who am I going to sue when I get knocked down?

00:02:19.709 --> 00:02:21.900
It's been banned in San Francisco.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:23.400
Which is particularly ironic,

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:26.300
because San Francisco always seems to be clamoring

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.100
for more transportation options.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.540
They're complaining about the traffic

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:30.960
and they're asking particularly

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.050
for green transportation options.

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:34.960
In San Francisco and many other cities,

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:37.659
scooter companies tried to escape

00:02:37.659 --> 00:02:39.459
destructive regulation

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:42.060
by doing what Uber and Airbnb did.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:43.407
Just put these out there,

00:02:43.407 --> 00:02:45.960
and hope that by the time the politicians notice,

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:46.800
the scooters

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.760
would be too popular to ban.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.010
They didn't get permission first.

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:52.500
And that's the issue.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:54.429
Unfortunately, cities haven't learned

00:02:54.429 --> 00:02:55.868
from their past experiences

00:02:55.868 --> 00:02:58.280
with companies like Uber and Airbnb,

00:02:58.280 --> 00:02:59.640
and they want these innovators

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:01.540
to come ask for permission and go through

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:03.280
the regulatory processes.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:04.460
Which can take years.

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:05.360
Which can take years,

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:07.220
and can also prevent consumers

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.180
from accessing a transportation option

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:10.980
that could be accessible now.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:13.080
San Francisco's now granted permits to

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:14.760
two small companies,

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:16.720
but not Lime and Bird,

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:19.180
the companies that started the business.

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:21.120
The pedestrians say they’re a hazard.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.320
They get up next to me and zoom right on by.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:24.760
Still, there are safety issues.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:28.160
This man reportedly died after falling off a scooter,

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:30.220
and some people ride recklessly.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:33.380
Excuse me, excuse me,  ahh f**k!

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:34.340
S**t.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:35.140
Are you OK?

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:37.099
They're gonna run us old people over!

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.560
We actually haven't seen a large number of accidents

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:41.780
or injuries with these scooters

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:43.549
Some people have been hurt.

00:03:43.549 --> 00:03:45.060
And some people get hurt,

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:46.920
but we don't see ourselves banning bicycles

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:49.920
because somebody might get hurt on a bicycle.

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:51.694
There will be social norms that evolve,

00:03:51.694 --> 00:03:53.340
just like we've seen with bike lanes.

00:03:53.349 --> 00:03:55.969
Then there’s the crazy opposition.

00:03:55.969 --> 00:03:59.860
Protestors say they think the deluge of electric scooters

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:02.320
in San Francisco is a symptom of

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:04.090
gentrification.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:05.660
This group's upset because

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:08.640
scooters are used by rich people, tech workers.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:12.360
The scooters have provoked intense anger here.

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:14.579
Some people throw scooters into the ocean,

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:16.500
others set scooters on fire.

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:20.060
People vandalize these.

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:22.079
It’s a low percentage of vandalism, though.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:24.080
I was just in another city the other day,

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.040
and we had 10,000 rides and we had

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:28.080
18 vandalism complaints.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.200
So, when you think about the amount of ridership.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:33.080
So, the irresponsible media blows this up.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.160
Whenever there’s something new,

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:37.759
the media always hype the problems.

00:04:37.759 --> 00:04:40.880
Some people call these scooters a nuisance.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.980
Which makes it odd that this city,

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:43.716
Washington,

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:45.180
welcomed scooters.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:46.860
What I love about the District is

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:49.640
they are letting us innovate in this space and

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:50.480
How can that be?

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:51.650
This is Washington, D.C.,

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:53.160
they regulate everything!

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:54.940
Well, they’re regulating us too, but

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:57.300
in a very responsible way.

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:59.540
Good for D.C.!

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:00.860
Not often I get to say that.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:02.480
One last twist:

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:03.560
So let's scan.

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:05.840
The scooters even create new ways to make money.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:07.000
Loading.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:07.780
Accept!

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:08.340
Accept!

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:09.350
We did it!

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:10.040
Yes!

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:11.738
When scooters lose battery power,

00:05:11.738 --> 00:05:14.311
scooter companies pay people, like this family,

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:15.300
to find them,

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:16.100
pick them up,

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:17.820
and charge them at home,

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:20.960
$5 to $20 dollars for every scooter they charge.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:22.699
What do you do with the money?

00:05:22.699 --> 00:05:26.759
Um, well I’m gonna try and invest.

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:28.220
So kids make money,

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:31.220
people have a new form of transport that’s green,

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:32.880
it's good exercise,

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.470
takes up less space than cars.

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:37.520
Maybe, just maybe,

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:40.590
the politicians will leave them alone.

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:42.620
Woohoo,

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:44.227
that’s a bad one

00:05:44.227 --> 00:05:45.740
right there boy!

